# Vitis HLS build output.
#
# Matched by shape, not by name. HLS writes one project directory per core at
# fpga/hls/<core>/<project>/ and regenerates every byte of it from the .cpp/.h
# /.tcl that sit alongside in fpga/hls/<core>/. This list used to name each
# project explicitly and went stale the moment qpsk_modem was split into the
# separate qpsk_demod and qpsk_mod projects: 127 MB of generated output was
# neither tracked nor ignored, and showed up as untracked noise on every
# status. A pattern cannot go stale that way.
#
# Source never lives two levels deep here, so nothing real is hidden. If that
# ever changes, `git add -f fpga/hls/<core>/<dir>` overrides this.
fpga/hls/*/*/
fpga/hls/*/logs/
fpga/hls/*/vitis-run.log
fpga/hls/*/build.log
baselines/

# Release artifacts. Bundles are large and reproducible from a tag; the golden
# copy lives in SDR_GOLDEN_MIRROR, not in git.
/out/
